	'k04f45d27' => 'Timber merchant, two yards',
	'k054a3631' => 'Public and products liability covers legal defense costs and third-party compensation when a customer, supplier, or member of the public suffers accidental injury or property damage arising from your operations or finished goods. It routinely leaves out pure financial losses without accompanying physical damage, work undertaken outside specified territorial limits, and incidents involving subcontractors who lack equivalent cover of their own. Insurers also enforce stringent conditions precedent regarding waste clearance and hot-work permits. During our yard walk, we ask: do visiting hauliers, contractors, and trade counter customers share active floor space with your forklifts, and are their access routes strictly separated?',
	'k0564255e' => 'A refrigerated food distributor employing 14 staff operated a busy distribution centre with high seasonal turnover. During our 90-minute site visit, we discovered their inventory declarations were calculated using a flat annual average rather than their peak autumn and holiday intake. Under their insurer\'s average clause, a major fire during peak season would have reduced their claim payout proportionally, leaving them underinsured by hundreds of thousands of euros. We restructured their placement onto an agreed seasonal stock clause, allowing inventory limits to flex automatically during peak months without incurring punitive year-round premiums or underinsurance penalties.',
	'k0590de96' => 'IN THEIR CASE',
	'k076fe6f4' => 'Who carries out the site visit?',
	'k07b595bb' => 'When you request a cover review or contact Hojo Brokers, we collect your name, commercial trading address, contact telephone number, email address, and existing insurance documentation. During our on-site survey, our risk surveyor notes physical characteristics of your premises, including construction materials, fire protection systems, security measures, and storage layouts. This data is collected solely to evaluate your risk exposures, prepare our written cover map, and negotiate terms with insurers if you request a market placement. We do not use your information for unrelated marketing purposes.',
	'k091ce55f' => 'We reply',
	'k09453598' => 'Document',
	'k096f7921' => 'ALL SIX COVERS',
	'k0aa56355' => 'Food distribution and refrigerated storage operations risk severe losses from refrigeration plant breakdown, refrigerant contamination, and seasonal inventory surges. Property and stock cover with seasonal clauses, business interruption, and machinery breakdown matter most. Typical policies fail when spoilage definitions require physical impact damage rather than thermostat failure, or when stock values peak during holiday trading. For example, a frozen produce wholesaler held stock valued at twice their annual average before festive deliveries, leaving €300,000 of palletised goods unhedged under standard average clauses before a seasonal endorsement was secured.',
	'k0b7cbec1' => 'BROKERS',
	'k0dd3cd55' => 'Warehousing and logistics facilities face chronic gaps regarding stock racking clearances, narrow aisle widths for reach trucks, and custodial liabilities for third-party freight.',
	'k0dd7a877' => 'Annual renewal review',
	'k107373e2' => 'Case 2',
	'k11289024' => 'What Details Should You Provide in Your Request?',
	'k12c9b7b2' => 'Renewal Notes',
	'k13ac3ea7' => 'A regional timber merchant operating across two industrial yards held an existing business interruption policy with a 6-month indemnity period. During our yard walk and discussions, the owner explained that their custom timber drying kiln was imported and required bespoke engineering. Rebuilding the kiln, obtaining environmental permissions, and completing commissioning would take approximately 14 months following a total loss. Had a fire occurred, their income protection would have ceased eight months before the yard could resume processing lumber. We renegotiated their policy to extend the indemnity period to match real-world replacement horizons.',
	'k13ece891' => '60 minutes, no obligation',
	'k13f15ede' => 'Our claims process follows three disciplined stages: Call, Document, and Settle. First, Call: you reach our Calder Bay office during office hours and speak directly with Tomas or an experienced broker who advises on immediate mitigation and formal notice obligations. Second, Document: we visit your site if necessary, record physical damage, compile inventory losses, and assemble documentary evidence before the insurer\'s adjuster arrives. Third, Settle: we negotiate the settlement scope, oversee interim payments for ongoing business interruption, and ensure final compensation is paid without delay.',
	'k1407e555' => 'Commercial insurance terms, policy warranties, and insurer risk appetites shift constantly across property, liability, and transit lines. Four times a year, Hojo Brokers publishes Renewal Notes, a concise newsletter written by our broking team in Calder Bay. We cover emerging exclusion clauses, statutory changes affecting premises liability, practical steps for managing seasonal stock surges, and checklist items to review before your annual renewal meeting. We avoid generic corporate marketing and focus entirely on actionable advice for businesses managing workshops, warehouses, and logistics fleets.',
	'k1503a165' => 'Ninety minutes on your floor.',
	'k157b2920' => 'Mara Hojo is the founder and principal broker of Hojo Brokers, leading the firm since 2009 with a technical focus on commercial property and business interruption risks. She works closely with business owners to ensure indemnity periods reflect real-world supply chain and rebuilding timelines. Daniel Okafor serves as senior broker, specialising in stock valuations, complex warehousing operations, and goods in transit. Daniel regularly assists transport operators and distribution hubs in aligning their declared inventory levels and carrier liability terms with their daily freight movements.',
	'k164908e8' => 'Contract print workshop, 9 staff',
	'k170e989f' => 'Our direct claims line is answered during regular office hours, Monday to Friday from 08:30 to 17:30. Every claim reported during office hours is acknowledged and acted upon the same day. For incidents occurring over weekends or outside standard working hours, we provide comprehensive emergency guidance on securing premises, preventing further water or weather ingress, and documenting the scene with photographs before our claims team opens at 08:30 on the next working morning.',
