	'k66cee693' => 'Wholesale operations and trade counters combine busy trade customer collection areas with active pallet racking and heavy vehicle traffic. Public liability, stock cover, and employers\' liability are crucial due to continuous interaction between customers, yard staff, and forklift plant. Gaps routinely occur when trade counter visitors wander into storage aisles or when cash handling limits are exceeded during morning contractor collections. For example, an electrical trade distributor allowed contractors to collect cable reels directly from storage aisles, exposing the business to major liability claims before physical barriers and separate trade counters were established.',
