	'k81814d89' => 'Employers\' liability protects your firm against statutory legal costs and damages when an employee, apprentice, or temporary worker sustains injury or illness during the course of their work. Policies often leave out contractual indemnities that exceed statutory requirements, injuries sustained by labour-only subcontractors whose supervision status is contested, and claims where mandatory health and safety training logs cannot be evidenced. During our yard inspection, we review operational staffing and ask: do temporary warehouse staff and agency drivers receive documented machine training before operating plant, and are their shift registers stored off-site for verification?',
	'k8202d154' => 'Most firms are insured. Fewer know for what.',
	'k82396803' => 'Each renewal',
	'k82f17ddc' => 'Commercial cover review',
	'k831388da' => 'Real commercial businesses encounter specific coverage flaws during ordinary operations. Here are three representative cases illustrating how our on-site cover review identified and corrected dangerous insurance gaps.',
	'k83402cf5' => 'Contact our Calder Bay office to schedule a site walk or discuss your current commercial insurance arrangements with an experienced broker.',
	'k8376ea83' => 'Visit and read',
	'k84891de6' => 'The indemnity period was lengthened to match the rebuild, and the firm now reviews it each renewal against the kiln\'s replacement lead time.',
	'k859ec11b' => 'Confidentiality and Data Retention',
	'k8621d55c' => 'Privacy Notice',
	'k87a1941a' => 'Tomas Becker',
	'k8a3d66f6' => 'Thank You for Your Request',
	'k8baa38b0' => 'SINCE 2009',
	'k8c9f8e22' => 'All physical and digital policy schedules, survey reports, and correspondence are held securely within our Calder Bay office systems. We do not sell, rent, or disclose your information to third parties, except to licensed insurers and underwriting agencies when obtaining quotation terms on your explicit instruction. In such cases, information is disclosed to 3–5 selected insurers under strict non-disclosure obligations. We retain client records in compliance with regulatory requirements, and you may request access to or deletion of your contact information at any time.',
	'k8e49b85d' => 'Within 2 working days',
	'k8ea59c2b' => 'When an incident occurs on your premises, Tomas Becker acts as your dedicated claims advocate. Tomas stays with you from the initial emergency call through site inspections, loss adjuster meetings, and document submissions, right through to final insurer settlement. Unlike traditional brokers who pass policyholders to third-party call centres, Tomas manages your file directly from our Calder Bay office. He ensures insurer loss adjusters receive accurate technical evidence, challenges unreasonable reservation-of-rights positions, and accelerates interim payments when cash flow is critical.',
	'k8fa62ea9' => 'Timber merchants and building material yards carry significant outdoor fire hazards, dust accumulation in sawmills, and extended recovery horizons for specialist drying kilns.',
	'k906bb5b3' => 'What Happens After You Ask for a Cover Review?',
	'k90f62f6c' => 'How Are Complaints Handled?',
	'k9194e9d0' => 'Map the Gaps',
	'k91ebb07d' => 'Transparent Fees and Commission',
	'k925ca596' => 'What Should You Have Ready for the Site Walk?',
	'k93f7d0d7' => 'Per month',
	'k9405a1e3' => 'Settle',
	'k9476267d' => 'Warehousing and logistics facilities face chronic gaps regarding stock racking clearances, narrow aisle widths for reach trucks, and custodial liabilities for third-party freight. Property, stock, and goods in transit covers matter most, alongside robust public liability for visiting hauliers. Standard policies fail when goods are stored higher than fire sprinklers allow or when overnight parking occurs outside fenced yards. For example, a third-party pallet distributor assumed carrier liability was handled by the haulier, discovering after a trailer fire that standard freight limits left two-thirds of the cargo uninsured.',
	'k94797b42' => 'Six covers, each read against your floor.',
	'k955f7151' => 'When you choose to place an insurance policy through Hojo Brokers, our exact commission percentage and cash figure are printed directly on every quote sheet alongside insurer net premiums. We obtain quotes from 3–5 insurers to ensure competitive terms, but we never accept undisclosed contingent commissions or volume bonuses that could compromise our independent advice. If you decide not to place cover through us, you owe nothing for your initial single-site review and you keep the written cover map to use as you see fit.',
	'k961df5b1' => 'How Is Broker Remuneration Handled?',
	'k96c24342' => 'Daniel Okafor',
	'k97630df2' => 'Business interruption cover replaces lost gross profit and funds ongoing standing charges such as wages, rent, and debt service when an insured property loss halts trading.',
	'k984ceac1' => 'Included',
	'k99dcbd52' => 'Goods in transit cover reimburses the cost of raw materials, parts, and finished products damaged, lost, or stolen while transported in your commercial vehicles or handled by third-party freight carriers. Standard policies typically exclude unattended overnight vehicle theft without approved immobilisers, driver negligence during loading, and goods moving under restrictive carrier conditions of carriage that limit recovery to statutory weight tariffs. As we examine your loading docks, we ask: who bears the contractual risk the moment loaded pallets leave your bay, and does your cover apply until the customer signs the delivery receipt?',
	'k9c06b01b' => 'We take terms from 3–5 independent commercial insurers and set their schedules side by side. Rather than lead with the premium, we compare deductibles, inner limits and operating conditions, so you can see how each underwriter reads your premises and your trade.',
	'k9c0cd68b' => 'A commercial contract print workshop employing 9 staff routinely held large volumes of expensive paper stock and custom metal plates delivered directly by print clients. Our physical review of the workshop floor revealed that these customer materials were stored alongside company inventory without distinct documentation. Their policy wording covered owned business contents but omitted a specific extension for goods in trust. In the event of a shop-floor fire or sprinkler discharge, the client-owned materials would have been completely excluded from settlement. We amended their schedule to explicitly incorporate full goods in trust cover.',
	'ka266a2f8' => 'Priya Raman and Tomas Becker',
	'ka38f8442' => 'What it costs',
	'ka3bdffd0' => 'What happens if we operate more than one site?',
	'ka4577132' => 'Visit 90 min + written map; commission disclosed if you place',
	'ka601490b' => 'Subscribe to Renewal Notes, our quarterly briefing written specifically for owners, directors, and operations managers of commercial facilities with physical premises.',
	'ka76d4ef5' => 'Time',
	'ka7812aea' => 'A mezzanine above the yard, since 2009.',
	'ka912e1ad' => 'These terms set out the basis on which Hojo Brokers provides commercial cover reviews and insurance broking services to corporate clients.',
	'kab949360' => 'Hojo Brokers is located on the 3rd floor at 18 Quayside Road in Calder Bay. We are open Monday to Friday from 08:30 to 17:30. Site visits to warehouses, workshops, and commercial premises are available Monday through Saturday by appointment, with Saturday visits scheduled from 09:00 to 13:00. We are closed on Sundays and public holidays. You can contact our office by telephone at +00 41 2290 6604 or by email at review@hojobrokers.example. Our office overlooks the commercial docklands, with visitor parking available behind the main building off Quayside Road.',
	'kabfcf041' => 'review@hojobrokers.example',
	'kac43e14a' => '<a class="hb-cell" href="/trades/#trade-1"><span class="hb-cell__t">Warehousing and logistics</span><span class="hb-cell__d">Racking heights, shared sites and other people\'s goods stored under your roof.</span></a>
<a class="hb-cell" href="/trades/#trade-2"><span class="hb-cell__t">Food distribution and cold store</span><span class="hb-cell__d">Spoilage after a power failure, refrigerant leaks and seasonal stock peaks.</span></a>
<a class="hb-cell" href="/trades/#trade-3"><span class="hb-cell__t">Light manufacturing</span><span class="hb-cell__d">Machinery breakdown, tooling on loan and the supplier whose failure stops your line.</span></a>
<a class="hb-cell" href="/trades/#trade-4"><span class="hb-cell__t">Timber and building supplies</span><span class="hb-cell__d">Fire spread across open yards, kiln rebuild times and stock stacked outdoors.</span></a>
<a class="hb-cell" href="/trades/#trade-5"><span class="hb-cell__t">Print and packaging workshops</span><span class="hb-cell__d">Customers\' paper and plates on your floor, and the dust and fire load around them.</span></a>
<a class="hb-cell" href="/trades/#trade-6"><span class="hb-cell__t">Wholesale and trade counters</span><span class="hb-cell__d">Walk-in customers, counter theft and stock that changes value through the year.</span></a>',
	'kac8ea4f9' => 'How Are Claims Reported During Office Hours?',
	'kad156c31' => 'The gaps we find most often, trade by trade.',
	'kae5734b0' => 'Employers\' Liability',
	'kae6b6ff7' => 'Goods in transit cover reimburses the cost of raw materials, parts, and finished products damaged, lost, or stolen while transported in your commercial vehicles or handled by third-party freight carriers.',
	'kaeebce66' => 'Priya Raman is our dedicated risk surveyor, conducting on-site engineering visits, sprinkler clearance assessments, and hazardous storage audits across industrial premises. Her detailed physical reports help clients resolve insurer survey requirements before binding terms. Tomas Becker is our dedicated claims advocate, providing hands-on representation whenever a client experiences an insured loss. Tomas stays with the client from the first notification call through loss adjusting meetings to final cash settlement, ensuring claims are handled promptly and fairly.',
	'kaf808a76' => 'About Hojo Brokers',
	'kaffa8f07' => 'The index',
	'kb0704e6c' => 'To help us prepare for your review, please tell us the physical address of each site you operate, the general nature of your trade, and your approximate renewal date. If you have your current insurance schedule and statement of fact available, you can attach them directly to your email. Do not worry if your documents are incomplete or spread across multiple policies; our broking team will review whatever records you currently hold and verify the physical details during our yard visit.',
	'kb1f0b866' => 'Cases',
	'kb27f46a5' => 'Ask for a cover review',
	'kb2a6410b' => 'Back in our Calder Bay office, our broking team reads your schedules clause by clause against our site notes. Within 10 working days, we produce a clear, written cover map. This diagnostic document sets out exactly what your current policies pay for, what exclusions leave your business exposed, where stock or equipment is underinsured, and which policy warranties are currently being breached in day-to-day operations. The cover map uses plain commercial language rather than legalistic broker jargon so you can clearly understand your firm\'s genuine insurance position.',
	'kb391a651' => 'Sofia Varga',
	'kb3b2a057' => 'We walk the full footprint of your premises with you instead of reading paper from a distant office. We check the clear height under sprinkler heads, the forklift aisles, pallets stacked against the boundary fence and where hazardous substances are kept, and we note the vehicles and visiting hauliers on site that your policy may not recognise.',
	'kb5d72fc9' => 'Confirmation and Review Scheduling',
	'kb64a9835' => 'Timber merchants and building material yards carry significant outdoor fire hazards, dust accumulation in sawmills, and extended recovery horizons for specialist drying kilns. Property cover, environmental liability, and business interruption with multi-year indemnity periods are critical. Typical policies fail because outdoor timber stacks violate boundary separation distances or dust extraction maintenance warranties are missed. For example, a timber merchant with two active yards carried six months of business interruption, discovering after an electrical blaze that sourcing and constructing an industrial drying kiln requires fourteen months from planning permit to operation.',
	'kb75b0ed0' => 'To help us evaluate your physical premises efficiently, please gather your current insurance policy schedule, statement of fact, and any recent risk improvement requirements issued by your existing insurer. If you operate multiple buildings or outdoor storage yards, ensure your operations manager is available to grant access to plant rooms, sprinkler valves, and electrical intake cupboards. There is no need to disrupt daily production or warehouse dispatch; observing your regular working operations is an essential part of identifying genuine insurance vulnerabilities.',
	'kb79d7efd' => 'Founded in 2009, Hojo Brokers is an independent commercial insurance broker based in Calder Bay. We specialise in advising small and mid-size firms operating warehouses, workshops, yards, and distribution facilities.',
	'kb9452775' => 'Our fees are agreed in advance and stay the same on every page of this site.',
	'kbb45b472' => '2–4 weeks',
	'kbbaff128' => 'Contact',
	'kbbdcd77b' => 'We are committed to delivering rigorous, professional broking standards to every commercial business we advise. If you have any cause for complaint regarding our review, advice, or administration, please contact Mara Hojo directly at our Calder Bay office by calling +00 41 2290 6604 or emailing review@hojobrokers.example. We acknowledge all complaints in writing within two working days during office hours and conduct an impartial investigation. Our claims advocacy service operates under identical standards of transparency, ensuring your interests are independently defended throughout any disputed insurance claim.',
	'kbceed0c1' => 'One request. We reply within two working days.',
	'kbf7c1f52' => 'We publish clear pricing for every independent review service we deliver. A first cover review for a single site costs €0; it includes our 90-minute on-site visit and a comprehensive written cover map, with broker commission disclosed if you choose to place cover through us. A multi-site review covering 2–5 sites takes 2–4 weeks and costs €480. A detailed contract wording read takes 5 working days and costs €160 per contract. An independent risk survey report based on a half-day site visit costs €320 for 1 visit. Our annual renewal review is included at each renewal for all active clients. Independent claims advocacy outside an active placement costs €90 per month.',
	'kbfaec778' => 'Timber and Building Supplies',
	'kc0241eae' => 'CONTACT',
	'kc10cd88b' => 'Until settled',
	'kc3755e61' => 'Call',
	'kc3a79a0d' => 'Warehousing and Logistics',
	'kc3c42cf7' => 'Visit and Read',
	'kc53aa070' => 'A first review costs nothing: we walk your site for 90 minutes, then show you in writing what your current cover does and does not pay for.',
	'kc5b29568' => 'Cold-store distributor, 14 staff',
	'kc5f29bb3' => 'Privacy',
	'kc6567352' => 'Commission and fees are disclosed in writing from the start. You receive the full comparison and our recommendation, with no obligation to place your cover through our office.',
	'kc6853cf9' => 'How many insurer quotes do you present?',
	'kc69366df' => 'We visit',
	'kced3d8a7' => 'CALL · DOCUMENT · SETTLE',
	'kced4de07' => 'Sofia Varga, our client service lead, will review your submission and contact you within two working days by phone or email. Sofia will confirm your site details, answer any immediate questions, and schedule our 90-minute on-site visit at a time convenient for your operations team. Site visits take place Monday to Friday between 08:30 and 17:30, or on Saturday mornings between 09:00 and 13:00. Once scheduled, a confirmation email with the visiting broker\'s details and a preliminary checklist will be sent directly to your inbox.',
	'kcf368ceb' => 'Read the risk before the policy.',
	'kcf9f9201' => 'Your initial single-site cover review includes an in-person 90-minute inspection of your physical premises, an exhaustive examination of your existing schedules, endorsements, and warranties, and the delivery of a written cover map within 10 working days. It concludes with a 60-minute consultation where we walk you through our findings, answer technical questions, and read key exclusions aloud. Every finding is backed by physical evidence observed on your premises, providing your management team with clear guidance on unhedged operational risks.',
	'kd051d9d0' => 'Same day',
	'kd070ce0f' => 'OFFICE HOURS',
	'kd0fbda98' => 'Page not found',
	'kd123008f' => 'Our cover review is an independent, three-stage diagnostic process designed for commercial operators with physical premises. We examine your actual operational site and existing policy documents before any market placement is considered.',
	'kd1802333' => 'First cover review, one site',
	'kd181b718' => 'What does the first cover review cost?',
	'kd62b5d69' => 'Cover map in 10 working days',
	'kd74eafe3' => 'Send us your current schedule and the address of each site. We will arrange a 90-minute walk of your yard and workshop at a time that suits your operations.',
	'kdab03558' => 'Timber Merchant, 2 Yards',
	'kdac69e59' => 'Food distribution and refrigerated storage operations risk severe losses from refrigeration plant breakdown, refrigerant contamination, and seasonal inventory surges.',
	'kdd1ba187' => 'News',
	'kde77e2ed' => 'Indemnity periods are often set at six or twelve months, although rebuilding a kiln or sourcing specialised parts takes well over a year. The same gap appears with goods in trust: customers\' materials on your floor are left out because a standard schedule only protects what your firm owns.',
	'kdf89e795' => 'THANKS',
	'kdf8a03ea' => 'Light manufacturing workshops frequently suffer from inadequate business interruption periods and uninspected machinery modifications. Business interruption, machinery breakdown, and employers\' liability are essential to protect bespoke production lines. Gaps routinely emerge when tooling dies, casting moulds, and proprietary jigs are destroyed and require custom fabrication from overseas manufacturers. For example, an assembly plant faced a six-month shut after a press motor burned out, but their business interruption policy expired after twelve weeks while replacement parts were still in transit from the original manufacturer.',
	'ke03eb8d4' => 'Every exclusion read aloud before you sign.',
	'ke16336e3' => 'Priya Raman',
	'ke1c8be89' => 'BEFORE THE WALK',
	'ke1d5d400' => 'Public and products liability covers legal defense costs and third-party compensation when a customer, supplier, or member of the public suffers accidental injury or property damage arising from your operations or finished goods.',
	'ke2a7a78a' => 'Senior broker; stock, warehousing, goods in transit.',
	'ke2e2b852' => 'How We Handle Your Subscription',
	'ke3284216' => 'Claims advocate; stays with the client from first call to settlement.',
	'ke4455101' => 'No fee for the first review. When you place cover through us, our commission is shown on every quote.',
	'ke4be1a3f' => 'Business interruption cover replaces lost gross profit and funds ongoing standing charges such as wages, rent, and debt service when an insured property loss halts trading. Standard wordings frequently exclude extended supply-chain disruption, utility failures off-premises, and rebuilding delays caused by planning approvals or long manufacturing lead times for imported machinery. Most schedules default to a twelve-month indemnity period, which sounds sufficient until specialised equipment must be engineered from scratch. When we survey your facility, we ask: if your primary processing line or drying equipment were destroyed tomorrow, how many months would re-ordering, shipping, installation, and commissioning realistically require?',
	'ke5b15040' => 'How a Cover Review Runs',
	'ke5c0cbb0' => 'Insurance is tested when a loss occurs on your premises. At Hojo Brokers, claims advocacy is handled personally by our dedicated specialist rather than outsourced call centres.',
	'ke5e5138f' => 'Contract Print Workshop, 9 Staff',
	'ke71f3909' => 'EVERY REVIEW FOLLOWS THE SAME THREE STEPS',
	'ke747cad0' => 'Placement Explained',
	'ke7ec5f63' => 'Public and Products Liability',
	'ke8488082' => 'By cover',
	'ke93d9005' => 'RENEWAL NOTES',
	'ke9df26dc' => 'Monday to Friday between 08:30 and 17:30, or on Saturdays from 09:00 to 13:00 by appointment.',
	'kea81bdb1' => 'How We Collect and Use Commercial Information',
	'kebc57247' => 'We have received your request for a commercial cover review. An independent broker from our Calder Bay office will contact you shortly to coordinate the next steps.',
	'kec2fc1c7' => 'We inspect physical premises and read existing policy schedules across six core commercial covers. Our reviews identify unhedged operational exposures, restrictive warranties, and dangerous gaps before an insured event occurs.',
	'ked397b8a' => 'Hojo · Okafor · Raman · Becker',
	'ked86a8a6' => 'Business Interruption',
	'ked86ba20' => 'Risk surveyor; site visits, sprinkler and storage reports.',
	'kf0096eb9' => 'Stock was declared at an average value, not the peak season. A seasonal stock clause was added.',
	'kf0c1f786' => 'TERMS OF BUSINESS',
	'kf32cf553' => 'Placement, in plain words',
	'kf37f271b' => 'ALL SIX TRADES',
	'kf546fd6d' => 'Four Practical Briefings a Year',
	'kf695d60c' => 'One advocate from first call to settlement.',
	'kf7b57f71' => 'A cover review runs through three stages without disturbing your working day.',
	'kf936d33a' => 'From the first walk to the cover map.',
	'kfa26401d' => 'What a review reads',
	'kfdc0e541' => 'Questions about a review',
	'kfdeb5e1b' => 'A short quarterly bulletin: practical policy changes and yard safety notes, with no sales pitch.',
	'kfe769807' => 'We believe commercial insurance broking should be entirely transparent. Our fee structure is published openly, and our broking remuneration is disclosed on every insurer quotation we provide.',
